WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.196
NIST SP 800-53 organizes controls into families.

00:00:03.196 --> 00:00:09.832
A control family groups related requirements and capabilities so the catalog is easier to navigate.

00:00:09.832 --> 00:00:13.813
Examples include Access Control, Audit and Accountability, Configuration Management,

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:17.352
Incident Response, Risk Assessment, System and Communications Protection,

00:00:17.352 --> 00:00:19.564
and System and Information Integrity.

00:00:19.564 --> 00:00:24.429
Other families address topics such as awareness and training, contingency planning,

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:27.526
identification and authentication, planning, privacy, personnel security,

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.738
and supply chain risk management.

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:35.046
Grouping controls into families helps organizations understand how safeguards relate to different

00:00:35.046 --> 00:00:37.700
areas of security and privacy management.
